{% set page_title = "Spain 29N polls · average, range and limits" %}
{% set page_desc = "Aggregated average of published polls for Spain's 29 November 2026 general election, with range, sources and limits. Not a forecast." %}
{% set canonical = site_url ~ "/en.html" %}
{% set page_lang = "en" %}
{% set jsonld = webpages['en.html'] %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
{% include "_head.html.j2" %}
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="topbar">
      <div class="brand">
        <span class="mark"></span>
        <span class="brandname"><a href="/">{{ site_name }}</a></span>
        <span class="tag">Spain · 29N 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="status">
        <a class="navpill" href="/">Español</a>
        <a class="navpill" href="/data/latest.json">Data JSON</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="container">
  <h1 style="margin:18px 0 4px;font-size:34px;letter-spacing:-0.03em">Spain 29N: polls, range and limits</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 16px">A minimal English summary of the <strong>29N</strong> observatory. The full site, sources and methodology are in Spanish. This is an aggregated average of published polls, not a forecast.</p>

  <div class="hero-kpis">
    <div class="hk"><b>{{ n_polls }}</b><span>polls in the average</span></div>
    <div class="hk"><b>{{ health.n_pollsters or "—" }}</b><span>polling houses</span></div>
    <div class="hk"><b>{{ days_to_election }}</b><span>days to election day</span></div>
    <div class="hk"><b>{{ days_to_blackout }}</b><span>days to polling blackout</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="stamp">Updated: <strong>{{ updated_at }}</strong> · last poll: <strong>{{ last_poll_date or "—" }}</strong> · sample declared in {{ health.sample_pct or 0 }}% of polls.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="cardhead"><h2>Current average</h2><span class="hint">range = observed polls, not a confidence interval</span></div>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Party</th><th>Average</th><th>Range</th><th>Median</th><th>Polls</th><th>Houses</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for p in parties_table[:7] %}
          <tr>
            <td><strong>{{ p.party }}</strong></td>
            <td class="num">{{ fmt_pct(p.mean) }}%</td>
            <td class="num">{{ fmt_pct(p.min) }}–{{ fmt_pct(p.max) }}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ fmt_pct(p.median) }}%</td>
            <td class="num">{{ p.n }}</td>
            <td class="num">{% if p.n_houses_window %}{{ p.n_houses_window }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted small">The average combines published polls with <strong>recency</strong> and <strong>declared sample size</strong> when available. The range is descriptive: it is not a confidence interval and is not a prediction.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="cardhead"><h2>What this is not</h2></div>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><strong>Not a forecast.</strong> It does not estimate the election result or seat distribution.</li>
      <li><strong>Not a single poll.</strong> It is a weighted average of polls published in the last 14 days.</li>
      <li><strong>Not demographically corrected.</strong> The site does not model age, sex, income or territory; sources may use quotas that are not published.</li>
      <li><strong>Not the full Congress.</strong> The hemicycle page applies national D'Hondt as a mechanical simulation; it is not the real provincial allocation and excludes regional parties.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="cardhead"><h2>Data and method</h2></div>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn" href="/data/latest.json">Latest JSON</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/data/status.json">Data status and hashes</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/data/v1/schema.json">JSON schema</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/metodologia.html">Method (ES)</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/fuentes.html">Sources (ES)</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/hemiciclo.html">Hemicycle (ES)</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/robustez.html">Robustness (ES)</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted small">Code: <a href="https://github.com/mcasrom/elecciones29n-osint" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AGPL-3.0</a> · contact: <a href="mailto:info.elecciones29n@pruebapublica.com">info.elecciones29n@pruebapublica.com</a> · {{ site_name }} v{{ version }} · {{ build_date }}.</p>
  </div>
</main>

<footer class="footer">
  <div class="container">
    <p>{{ site_name }} · aggregated average of published polls for Spain's 29 November 2026 general election.</p>
    <p><a href="/">Español</a> · <a href="/caveat.html">Limits (ES)</a> · <a href="/privacidad.html">Privacy (ES)</a> · <a href="/apoyo.html">Support</a></p>
  </div>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
